{{!--
  Two shapes of the same email. `isInvitationAccepted` is "true" when a master
  admin ticked "accept the invitation automatically" on the invite form: the
  membership is already accepted, so there is nothing for the recipient to
  accept, and telling them to go and accept it would send them looking for an
  invitation that is not there.

  `ifCond` compares two values and takes no boolean operators, so the isNewUser
  split is nested inside each branch rather than combined. The `else` arms keep
  the original invitation wording for anything that does not set the variable.
--}}

{{#ifCond isInvitationAccepted "true"}}

{{> EmailTitle title=(concat "🎉 You've Been Added to " projectName) }}

{{#ifCond isNewUser "true"}}
{{> InfoBlock info="You've been added to a project on OneUptime. Create your account to get started - your access is already waiting for you."}}

{{> ButtonBlock buttonUrl=registerLink buttonText="Create Your Account"}}

{{> VerticalSpace this}}

{{> InfoBlock info="Or copy and paste this link into your browser:"}}
{{> InfoBlock info=registerLink}}
{{else}}
{{> InfoBlock info="You've been added to a project on OneUptime. Sign in to get started - there is nothing for you to accept."}}

{{> ButtonBlock buttonUrl=signInLink buttonText="Sign In to OneUptime"}}

{{> VerticalSpace this}}

{{> InfoBlock info="Or copy and paste this link into your browser:"}}
{{> InfoBlock info=signInLink}}
{{/ifCond}}

{{else}}

